<%# How to play. Server-rendered so its rules are in the page for search engines; HowToPlay.tsx opens it and adds the example set. %>
<dialog id="how-to-play" aria-labelledby="how-to-play-title" class="fixed inset-0 m-0 h-dvh max-h-none w-full max-w-none items-center justify-center overflow-hidden border-0 bg-transparent p-3 pb-[calc(env(safe-area-inset-bottom,0px)+0.75rem)] open:flex backdrop:bg-neutral-900/40 backdrop:backdrop-blur-[2px] sm:p-6 dark:backdrop:bg-black/60">
  <div class="animate-dialog-in relative flex max-h-full w-full max-w-sm flex-col overflow-y-auto overscroll-contain rounded-2xl border border-neutral-200 bg-white px-5 pb-5 pt-4 text-neutral-900 shadow-2xl dark:border-neutral-700 dark:bg-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-100">
    <form method="dialog">
      <button type="submit" aria-label="Close" class="absolute right-2 top-2 flex h-9 w-9 cursor-pointer items-center justify-center rounded-full text-neutral-400 transition-colors hover:bg-neutral-100 hover:text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-500 dark:hover:bg-neutral-800 dark:hover:text-neutral-200">
        <svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" class="h-4 w-4"><path d="M6 6l12 12M18 6 6 18"/></svg>
      </button>
    </form>
    <h2 id="how-to-play-title" class="text-center text-base font-semibold">How to play</h2>
    <div id="rules-demo-root" class="mt-3"></div>
    <p class="mt-3 text-balance text-center text-sm text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-300">Find 3 cards: each feature all same or all different.</p>
    <div class="mt-4 border-t border-neutral-100 pt-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-neutral-600 dark:border-neutral-800 dark:text-neutral-400">
      <ul class="space-y-1.5">
        <li>Every card has four features: number, color, shape and shading.</li>
        <li>Three cards are a set when each feature is either the same on all three cards or different on all three.</li>
        <li>Tap three cards to claim a set.</li>
      </ul>
      <dl class="mt-4 grid grid-cols-[auto_1fr] gap-x-3 gap-y-1.5">
        <dt class="font-medium text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-100">Daily Deal</dt><dd>Same deal for everyone, one try a day.</dd>
        <dt class="font-medium text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-100">Puzzle</dt><dd>12 cards hold 6 sets. Find all 6.</dd>
        <dt class="font-medium text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-100">Practice</dt><dd>Timed games, as many as you like.</dd>
        <dt class="font-medium text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-100">Multiplayer</dt><dd>Most sets wins the round.</dd>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </div>
</dialog>
<%# The longer description, kept in the page for search engines and screen readers, out of sight. %>
<section class="sr-only" aria-labelledby="about-set-title">
  <h2 id="about-set-title">About Set</h2>
  <p>
    Set is a fast visual puzzle played with a deck of 81 cards: spot three cards that form a set before anyone else does.
    Play it free in your browser, with a Daily Deal and a daily Puzzle that are the same for everyone, timed practice games with daily, weekly and monthly leaderboards, or on a live shared board with friends.
  </p>
  <h3>Rules</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Every card has four features: number (one, two or three), color (red, purple or green), shape (diamond, oval or squiggle) and shading (solid, striped or open).</li>
    <li>Tap three cards to claim a set. Twelve cards are showing, and more are dealt when there is no set on the board.</li>
    <li>Daily Deal: everyone gets the same deal; clear the whole deck as fast as you can, with one ranked try a day and a new deal at midnight Pacific.</li>
    <li>Puzzle: 12 cards hold exactly 6 sets (cards can be in more than one); find all 6. A new puzzle every midnight Pacific.</li>
    <li>Practice: timed games against the clock, as many as you like. Multiplayer: whoever finds the most sets wins the round.</li>
  </ul>
</section>
